          ],
          "content": "Arithmetic Expressions"
        },
        {
          "type": "doc_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.093,
            0.573,
            0.114
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "content": "1T'5 PUZZLE TIME!"
        },
        {
          "type": "doc_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.411,
            0.127,
            0.642,
            0.148
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "content": "Expression Engineer!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.178,
            0.834,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": "Using three 3’s along with the four operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division) and brackets as needed we can create several expressions. For example, (3 + 3)/3 = 2, 3 + 3 – 3 = 3, 3 × 3 + 3 = 12, and so on."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.252,
            0.834,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "Using four 4’s, create expressions to get all values from 1 to 20. Using the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 exactly once in any order get as many values as possible between  – 10 and +10."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.307,
            0.834,
            0.343
          ],
          "content": "Using the numbers 0 to 9 exactly once in any order, make an expression with a value 100."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.344,
            0.728,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "What other similar interesting questions can you ask?"
        },
